# Every path, one owner. This repository ships an unsigned executable that
# requests Administrator and writes to HKLM, so the review question on an
# outside pull request is not "is this good code" but "is this something I am
# willing to sign my name to and hand a user's machine to". One catch-all rule
# answers that for every file, including files nobody has thought of yet.
#
# Kept as a single line on purpose. Per-directory owners on a solo project only
# create paths that fall through the cracks when a directory is renamed.
